[?2004hroot@64877bd11e71:/app# bash /opt/gnomon-run.sh 'Spin up a mailing list server for our reading group: reading-group@local.edu using postfix and mailman3 (both are installed already).
[?2004l[?2004h> The mailing list has basic mailman3 functionalities like:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Mailing "reading-group-join@local.edu" adds users to the list (after confirmation).
[?2004l[?2004h> - Mailing "reading-group-leave@local.edu" removes users from the list (after confirmation).
[?2004l[?2004h> - Mailing "reading-group@local.edu" posts an announcement to all subscribers.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> You must save mailman configuration file in /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> For ease of testing:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Assume all subscriber/user mail addresses follow `<user>@local.edu`, where `<user>` is the local unix username.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Direct user mails to `/var/mail/<username>`. They will be accessed with `mailbox.mbox(f"/var/mail/{username}")`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - List owners do not need to approve join/post requests, i.e., set SubscriptionPolicy.open. Users still need to confirm join/leave by replying though.
